WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:05.116
The army is a pool; the combo is a table.

00:00:05.116 --> 00:00:08.432
The README, read against the code at 5702d90.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.821
The README, from voxel-musou: Dense voxel crowds of Wei soldiers (~300, InstancedMesh)

00:00:15.821 --> 00:00:18.539
blasted apart into voxel debris.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.628
84 soldiers the director keeps on the hero, at any army size.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:29.245
Crowd buffers re-uploaded every frame, upper bound.

00:00:29.245 --> 00:00:33.270
?enemies=300, 0.43 MB; ?enemies=2000, 2.80 MB.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:39.307
Arithmetic on buffer capacities; the game was not run.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:45.492
25 26 24 26 35 frames between the six strikes, counted

00:00:45.492 --> 00:00:47.380
from the move table.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.612
Accurate, in a narrower sense than it reads.

00:00:50.612 --> 00:00:51.768
The feel is data.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:59.108
Every number here is from the full article, with its sources, at ai.thesatyajit.com.
